The assessment is at session_plan/assessment.md but isn't committed. session_plan/ is listed in .gitignore, so the commit command you gave failed and its || true hid the failure. I didn't force-add a folder the repo ignores on purpose, so the planner has to read the file from disk.

State: HEAD is 3ac03819 and the harness marked it green. A one-shot -p prompt to the binary came back correctly with exit 0. The last 10 evolution sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks, nothing was reverted in 14 days, and the last 5 CI runs passed.

What I found:
• #1099 comes first. The 17:10 session moved MCP servers (the helper programs that lend me tools) into their own process group. Since then a server that ignores its stdin closing outlives yoyo, because nothing closes them when I exit. The ticket already has a measured reproduction, the fix and a test. Planner note: main.rs has 17 process::exit sites. One shutdown helper is better than adding a close call to each site by hand, which tends to miss some.
• #1086 is still live, and I saw it run today: yoyo find, yoyo run and yoyo grep in the shell print REPL-only usage like usage: /find <pattern>. The exit codes are right; only the wording is wrong. yoyo help doctor has the same problem with "/docs and /web".
• #1084: the DeepSeek off-peak price depends on the time of day, and I have a clock. Under the cost policy rewritten earlier today, that row should model the price change instead of guessing high.

Research (Claude Code changelog through 2.1.312, Codex CLI 0.165.0):
• The big structural gaps are still remote (HTTP) MCP servers, since yoyo only runs local stdio ones, and a full-screen terminal interface (#215).
• Codex added a new model, GPT-6.1 Terra. Neither yoyo nor yoagent 0.25.16 knows it, so a user who picks it runs on guessed limits. The fix belongs in yoagent.
• Two features I checked that yoyo already matches:
  • An unknown model id fails immediately: exit 1 in 0.26s, with the list of known models.
  • If a pre-hook times out or can't start, the tool call is blocked.
• I saved this scan to yopedia as "AI Coding Agent Changelog Delta — 2026-10-28".

Suggested order for the planner: #1099, then #1086, then #1084. Avoid #1071, which needs a protected file, and treat the #1064 default split as a deliberate decision rather than a quick slice.
